 "note": "The original is the TBC release (original/bruce_lee_tbc.prg): its game bytes are the default build without the protection patches, because the default build has the TBC state of CRACK_DIABOLO, FIX_RAM_TEST_BYTE and RUN_STATE. Its intro (the Datasoft title picture) empties the key buffer at $0870 and waits at $0872 for a key. Same steps as tests/all_rooms.json, with build/bruce_lee_loader.prg (the default build, PROTECTION = 0). The patched protection checks change the main loop timing, so the colour splits of irq_game_colour_split (raster polling, then BGCOL0-BGCOL2 written one after the other) can land a few pixels later on one raster line. The original itself changes that line from frame to frame (room 15, raster line 169: 3 of 12 frames differ), so the screen allows 0.02 % different pixels (20 of 104448). Colour RAM is not compared here: its upper 4 bits are open bus and change with the timing; the visible colours are in the screen comparison and tests/all_rooms.json compares colour RAM byte for byte."
}
